  32:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  33:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  34:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     [..]
  35:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Initialize the JPEG peripheral using HAL_JPEG_Init : No initialization parameters are requ
  36:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          Only the call to HAL_JPEG_Init is necessary to initialize the JPEG peripheral.
  37:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  38:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) If operation is JPEG encoding use function HAL_JPEG_ConfigEncoding to set
  39:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          the encoding parameters (mandatory before calling the encoding function).
  40:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          the application can change the encoding parameter ImageQuality from
  41:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          1 to 100 to obtain a more or less quality (visual quality vs the original row image),
  42:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          and inversely more or less jpg file size.
  43:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  44:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Note that for decoding operation the JPEG peripheral output data are organized in
  45:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          YCbCr blocks called MCU (Minimum Coded Unit) as defioned in the JPEG specification
  46:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          ISO/IEC 10918-1 standard.
  47:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          It is up to the application to transform these YCbCr blocks to RGB data that can be displa
  48:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  49:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          Respectively, for Encoding operation the JPEG peripheral input should be organized
  50:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          in YCbCr MCU blocks. It is up to the application to perform the necessary RGB to YCbCr
  51:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          MCU blocks transformation before feeding the JPEG peripheral with data.
  52:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  53:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Use functions HAL_JPEG_Encode and HAL_JPEG_Decode to start respectively
  54:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          a JPEG encoding/decoding operation in polling method (blocking).
  55:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  56:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Use functions HAL_JPEG_Encode_IT and HAL_JPEG_Decode_IT to start respectively
  57:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          a JPEG encoding/decoding operation with Interrupt method (not blocking).
  58:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  59:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Use functions HAL_JPEG_Encode_DMA and HAL_JPEG_Decode_DMA to start respectively
  60:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          a JPEG encoding/decoding operation with DMA method (not blocking).
  61:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  62:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_InfoReadyCallback is asserted if the current operation
  63:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          is a JPEG decoding to provide the application with JPEG image  parameters.
  64:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          This callback is asserted when the JPEG peripheral successfully parse the
  65:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          JPEG header.
  66:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  67:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_GetDataCallback is asserted for both encoding and decoding
  68:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          operations to inform the application that the input buffer has been
  69:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          consumed by the peripheral and to ask for a new data chunk if the operation
  70:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (encoding/decoding) has not been complete yet.
  71:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  72:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****         (++) This CallBack should be implemented in the application side. It should
  73:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              call the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer if new input data are available,
  74:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              or call HAL_JPEG_Pause with parameter XferSelection set to JPEG_PAUSE_RESUME_INPUT
  75:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              to inform the JPEG HAL driver that the ongoing operation shall pause waiting for the
  76:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              application to provide a new input data chunk.
  77:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              Once the application succeed getting new data and if the input has been paused,
  78:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              the application can call the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer to set the new
  79:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              input buffer and size, then resume the JPEG HAL input by calling new function HAL_JPEG
  80:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              If the application has ended feeding the HAL JPEG with input data (no more input data)
  81:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              Should call the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer (within the callback HAL_JPEG_GetD
  82:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****              with the parameter InDataLength set to zero.
  83:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  84:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (++) The mechanism of HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer/HAL_JPEG_Pause/HAL_JPEG_Resume allows
  85:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               to the application to provide the input data (for encoding or decoding) by chunks.
  86:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               If the new input data chunk is not available (because data should be read from an inp
  87:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               for example) the application can pause the JPEG input (using function HAL_JPEG_Pause)
  88:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               Once the new input data chunk is available ( read from a file for example), the appli
ARM GAS  C:\Users\nicx5\AppData\Local\Temp\ccxhjjXf.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               can call the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer to provide the HAL with the new chun
  90:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               then resume the JPEG HAL input by calling function HAL_JPEG_Resume.
  91:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (++) The application can call functions HAL_JPEG_ConfigInputBuffer then HAL_JPEG_Resume.
  93:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               any time (outside the HAL_JPEG_GetDataCallback)  Once the new input chunk data availa
  94:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               However, to keep data coherency, the function HAL_JPEG_Pause must be imperatively cal
  95:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               (if necessary) within the callback HAL_JPEG_GetDataCallback, i.e when the HAL JPEG ha
  96:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               Transferring the previous chunk buffer to the JPEG peripheral.
  97:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
  98:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_DataReadyCallback is asserted when the HAL JPEG driver
  99:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          has filled the given output buffer with the given size.
 100:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 101:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (++) This CallBack should be implemented in the application side. It should
 102:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               call the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigOutputBuffer to provide the HAL JPEG driver
 103:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               with the new output buffer location and size to be used  to store next data chunk.
 104:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               if the application is not ready to provide the output chunk location then it can
 105:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               call the function HAL_JPEG_Pause with parameter XferSelection set to JPEG_PAUSE_RESUM
 106:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               to inform the JPEG HAL driver that it shall pause output data. Once the application
 107:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               is ready to receive the new data chunk (output buffer location free or available) it 
 108:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               the function HAL_JPEG_ConfigOutputBuffer to provide the HAL JPEG driver
 109:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               with the new output chunk buffer location and size, then call HAL_JPEG_Resume
 110:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               to inform the HAL that it shall resume outputting data in the given output buffer.
 111:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 112:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (++) The mechanism of HAL_JPEG_ConfigOutputBuffer/HAL_JPEG_Pause/HAL_JPEG_Resume allows
 113:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               the application to receive data from the JPEG peripheral by chunks. when a chunk
 114:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               is received, the application can pause the HAL JPEG output data to be able to process
 115:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               these received data (YCbCr to RGB conversion in case of decoding or data storage in c
 116:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               of encoding).
 117:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 118:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          (++) The application can call  functions HAL_JPEG_ ConfigOutputBuffer then HAL_JPEG_Resume
 119:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               any time (outside the HAL_JPEG_DataReadyCallback) Once the output data buffer is free
 120:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               However, to keep data coherency, the function HAL_JPEG_Pause must be imperatively cal
 121:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               (if necessary) within the callback HAL_JPEG_ DataReadyCallback, i.e when the HAL JPEG
 122:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****               Transferring the previous chunk buffer from the JPEG peripheral to the application.
 123:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 124:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_EncodeCpltCallback is asserted when the HAL JPEG driver has
 125:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          ended the current JPEG encoding operation, and all output data has been transmitted
 126:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          to the application.
 127:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 128:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_DecodeCpltCallback is asserted when the HAL JPEG driver has
 129:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          ended the current JPEG decoding operation. and all output data has been transmitted
 130:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          to the application.
 131:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 132:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) Callback HAL_JPEG_ErrorCallback is asserted when an error occurred during
 133:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          the current operation. the application can call the function HAL_JPEG_GetError()
 134:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          to retrieve the error codes.
 135:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 136:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****      (#) By default the HAL JPEG driver uses the default quantization tables
 137:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          as provide in the JPEG specification (ISO/IEC 10918-1 standard) for encoding.
 138:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          User can change these default tables if necessary using the function HAL_JPEG_SetUserQuant
 139:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          Note that for decoding the quantization tables are automatically extracted from
 140:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****          the JPEG header.
 141:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 142:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****       (#) To control JPEG state you can use the following function: HAL_JPEG_GetState()
 143:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
