 158:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
 159:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   =============================================
 160:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 161:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   The compilation define  USE_HAL_JPEG_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 162:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 163:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   Use Functions HAL_JPEG_RegisterCallback() or HAL_JPEG_RegisterXXXCallback()
 164:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   to register an interrupt callback.
 165:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 166:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   Function HAL_JPEG_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 167:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) EncodeCpltCallback : callback for end of encoding operation.
 168:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) DecodeCpltCallback : callback for end of decoding operation.
 169:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback      : callback for error detection.
 170:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback    : JPEG MspInit.
 171:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback  : JPEG MspDeInit.
 172:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 173:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   and a pointer to the user callback function.
 174:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 175:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   For specific callbacks InfoReadyCallback, GetDataCallback and DataReadyCallback use dedicated
 176:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   register callbacks : respectively HAL_JPEG_RegisterInfoReadyCallback(),
 177:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   HAL_JPEG_RegisterGetDataCallback() and HAL_JPEG_RegisterDataReadyCallback().
 178:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 179:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   Use function HAL_JPEG_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 180:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   weak function.
 181:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   HAL_JPEG_UnRegisterCallback() takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 182:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   and the Callback ID.
 183:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 184:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) EncodeCpltCallback : callback for end of encoding operation.
 185:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) DecodeCpltCallback : callback for end of decoding operation.
 186:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback      : callback for error detection.
 187:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback    : JPEG MspInit.
 188:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback  : JPEG MspDeInit.
 189:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 190:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   For callbacks InfoReadyCallback, GetDataCallback and DataReadyCallback use dedicated
 191:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   unregister callbacks : respectively HAL_JPEG_UnRegisterInfoReadyCallback(),
 192:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   HAL_JPEG_UnRegisterGetDataCallback() and HAL_JPEG_UnRegisterDataReadyCallback().
 193:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
 194:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   By default, after the HAL_JPEG_Init() and when the state is HAL_JPEG_STATE_RESET
 195:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions :
 196:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   examples HAL_JPEG_DecodeCpltCallback() , HAL_JPEG_GetDataCallback().
 197:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 198:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   reset to the legacy weak function in the HAL_JPEG_Init()/ HAL_JPEG_DeInit() only when
 199:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 200:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   if not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_JPEG_Init() / HAL_JPEG_DeInit()
 201:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c ****   keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit functions (registered beforehand)
 202:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_jpeg.c **** 
